4. Mini Troubleshooting Flow

When a service (like SSH or Docker) stops functioning, follow this standard step-by-step workflow:
1.Check system process status:
Rule out crashed processes.
Verify whether the binary process itself is alive.
pgrep -l sshd
|
2.Inspect service state:
Identify systemd failures.
Check systemd service health to see if it crashed, failed to start, or timed out.
systemctl status ssh
|
3.Filter logs for errors:
Find root cause.
Query systemd journal logs specifically for error flags or panic messages.
sudo journalctl -u ssh -p err..emerg -n 20
|
4.Attempt a controlled restart:
Apply fix and test.
Restart the service and monitor its status in real-time.
sudo systemctl restart ssh && systemctl status ssh

 
